## Summary

Shipped the native Apple (SwiftUI) parity of the web `FullscreenButton` primitive at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/FullscreenButton.*` — 8 files following the established `CopyButton` convention:

- **`.Model.swift`** — surface slug + `view.opened` telemetry seam (P1/S11), pure logic (glyph/label/active-detection/4-way toggle decision ported verbatim from the web branches), i18n facade, and the `@MainActor @Observable` state-holder (P1/S8).
- **`.Seams.swift`** — `FullscreenPresenting` (the observable native shape of the browser Fullscreen API) + production and in-memory presenters.
- **`.swift` / `.Views.swift`** — the `TSButton`-based surface + the symbol-swap label (Reduce-Motion aware, VoiceOver-correct).
- **`.Previews.swift`** — every state (resting, active, custom labels, detached, unsupported, live demo).
- **`.Tests.swift` / `.ModelTests.swift`** — 40 tests (logic, view-state, a11y, i18n, diagnostics, support, live-state, toggle-flow).
- **`.strings`** — the two `common.fullscreen.*` keys verbatim.

**Every web branch reproduced**: support-gate hide, `fullscreenchange`-sourced state, descendant detection, exit-then-request arbitration, rejection handling, label/icon/aria-pressed flip, enter/exit overrides. The generic data-feed states are intentionally absent (stateless/networkless primitive — the documented CopyButton/ChartExportMenu precedent).

**Gate results (all real):**
- `LINT_EXIT=0` (0 violations / 4670 files), `FORMAT_EXIT=0` (0/4968), `PLACEHOLDER_EXIT=0`, `XCODEGEN_EXIT=0`
- `SWIFT_TEST_EXIT=0` — 39/39 logic tests green (Swift 6 strict concurrency), verbatim Model+Seams
